# Normalise line endings across Windows and macOS.
#
# Without this, git stores whatever each machine commits. Editing a file on
# the Mac that was committed from Windows (or vice versa) can rewrite every
# line in the file, producing diffs where nothing actually changed and making
# `git blame` useless.
#
# text=auto  — treat files as text and store LF in the repository
# eol=lf     — check out LF in the working tree on every platform
#
# LF everywhere is standard for JS/TS projects and is what Node, Next, and
# every modern editor expect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be line-ending converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
